{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/22059-some-thoughts-of-cover-and-compromise","id":22059,"title":"Some thoughts of Cover and Compromise","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-02T19:06:28-08:00","id":22059,"title":"Some thoughts of Cover and Compromise","content":"I find myself thinking... If a demon's original cover as an Angel was add a serial killer, does refraining from murdering someone who fits their profile count toward compromise? Or say, an Angel was positioned as a hospital worker, with the task of killing undesirables who come in (like stigmatics who don't serve the God Machine or other nuisances). They're doing a lot of murder by intentional malpractice, and probably doing it in human rather than angelic form, so does that necessarily get worked into the Cover the demon inherits from its pre fallen state? Or since Angels don't worry about Compromise. Can the Demon &quot;safely&quot; abandon that part of its history? I'm hoping for this to be a 'discussion' thing rather than an official ruling - it seems like something that should be between player and ST - but would of course love to hear dev opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T19:48:08-08:00","id":22071,"title":"","content":"Related thing from the old Demon blog:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so, you might ask, does that mean I can make a character whose character is a serial killer and not lose Cover for committing murder? And the answer is, <i>what is wrong with you and why would you ask that?</i> </div> </div> </div>We'll see if there are any more in-depth thoughts in a dedicated topic, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 12-02-2013, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T20:49:58-08:00","id":22099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/22059-some-thoughts-of-cover-and-compromise?p=22071#post22071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related thing from the old Demon blog:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We'll see if there are any more in-depth thoughts in a dedicated topic, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I vaguely recalled that. My question is more interested in a Demon who got such a Cover thrust upon them, and doesn't want to be that person anymore - is that basically a ticking time bomb for them?.<br /> A Soul Pact is one way out of that, but that also can involve discarding some very useful aspects of the otherwise distasteful cover. It certainly is aspiration-fodder to try and find a fitting one, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T20:52:14-08:00","id":22100,"title":"","content":"I actually think it'd be more prudent for a demon with that predilection to ditch it as there's no guarantee the GM wouldn't pick up on a task still being worked on.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">As players, we know that a demon's Cover and everything connected cauterizes after disconnecting. The GM and its angels doesn't automatically know what the demon does. But conventional hiding would be &quot;Don't do what I did before,&quot; or at the least readjust the routine.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">So the Kevorkian nurse leaves that hospital and takes up maybe at a free clinic, still administering to sick people but not killing them. An organic solution to the spirit of Cover I think. Unless I've missed the implications.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Alternately, wouldn't or couldn't that be written out of reality? The Fall tears at the foundations of everything in relation to the demon falling. Unless the job is literally &quot;serial killer&quot; and not subordinate to what would be a normal job, i.e. nurse, I'd assume it gets written out.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The only way I could see &quot;serial killer&quot; as a primary job would be if it's supported by stealing the victim's ID and trying to appropriate his or her life. But in that case, why not have that demon be a pathological Pact maker. Maybe he's compelled to assimilate people and use them up or in an extremely misanthropic mood he does it because he knows that person ceases to be forever. No spirit, no memories, nothing to indicate the person ever was. But that sounds more like a Hunter antagonist than a viable PC. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Would definitely like to know what a dev thinks about this question for default assumption.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","name":"Calrabjohns","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T05:15:14-08:00","id":22274,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Right now, I'd have the Destroyer who'd been positioned like that moving on quickly to a different hospital and not having the murder-y bit follow along as part of the Cover. I found myself musing that maybe she shouldn't be able to slip that so completely, but yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T20:12:30-08:00","id":22850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Hat Matt addressed this in the <a href=\"http://www.reddit.com/r/rpg/comments/1rl8vy/we_are_onyx_path_publishing_publishers_of_white/cdoeqko\" target=\"_blank\">AMA</a>:</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not the question I'm asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T21:31:31-08:00","id":22891,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine that a Cover who is a serial killer would actually risk Compromise for not killing on at least a semi-regular basis.<br /> <br /> As far as an Angel who pretends to be a Nurse who then kills patients; You could go either way depending on how you want the story to go.<br /> <br /> When the fall comes, you could say she was just a Nurse and it was the Demon's duty to kill but the Infrastructure that supports the Cover just smooths everything over perfectly. Or you could say that the Cover actually is a Serial Killer Nurse and then the Demon has to deal with either killing or risking their cover degrading. Either option is equally valid. Whichever story you want to tell is the one you should go with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1178-ravenmancer","name":"Ravenmancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T08:28:19-08:00","id":23165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/22059-some-thoughts-of-cover-and-compromise#post22059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find myself thinking... If a demon's original cover as an Angel was add a serial killer, does refraining from murdering someone who fits their profile count toward compromise? Or say, an Angel was positioned as a hospital worker, with the task of killing undesirables who come in (like stigmatics who don't serve the God Machine or other nuisances). They're doing a lot of murder by intentional malpractice, and probably doing it in human rather than angelic form, so does that necessarily get worked into the Cover the demon inherits from its pre fallen state? Or since Angels don't worry about Compromise. Can the Demon &quot;safely&quot; abandon that part of its history? I'm hoping for this to be a 'discussion' thing rather than an official ruling - it seems like something that should be between player and ST - but would of course love to hear dev opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case another question comes up though. Was it part of the cover (the killing) or part of the task of the angel.<br /> As I read it it was more part of the angels task not the cover. The cover is hospital worker. The &quot;mission&quot; the angel had and thus did was not part of the cover itself, thus the killing would not be a part of the cover.<br /> <br /> but for the original question: If it is an integral part of the cover, then it would cause compromise if you dont enact it. For example if your cover is hannibal lecter and dont kill anyone, or if you dont use his modi operandi for the killings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T08:45:05-08:00","id":23175,"title":"","content":"Ah, my ST found the thread. Good, that's how I was hoping to go with it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}